{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492109-need-informations-on-dementation","id":1492109,"title":"Need informations on Dementation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-01T12:54:44-07:00","id":1492109,"title":"Need informations on Dementation","content":"I'm happy none of my pc chose malkavian, dementation is annoying me. Here's my problems:<br /> 1) This discipline has no weakness, Domination only work with visual contact, obfuscate does not affect technologie, even presence can be countered by spending willpower<br /> <br /> 2) Used by pc it's great but when npc use it on pc (especially new pc) the effects can last for a long time during wich pc can do nothing more than suffer the effects (total insanity used by a sabbat member on a new pc with 5/6 willpower can be... disastrous<br /> <br /> 3) Even without weakness, deal with psychological transformation cannot be just a temporary modification with a countdown clock after wich no more effect at all. A victim of Dementation should not be sure that he's under influence of a power, the question he will ask himslef about his own sanity and if his reactions are normal or not should be the essence of dementation. Malkavian would torture their victim by making them doubt about evrything about themself until a point their victim does not need dementation to go mad anymore.<br /> <br /> So how do you handle it in your game? Is there some information i'm missing as i only have V20 book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 09-01-2022, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T13:02:40-07:00","id":1492112,"title":"","content":"Not sure what information are you looking for. These just appear to be complaints.<br /> <br /> Now they are complaints that I share. Among my personal gaming groups, I don't know anybody who likes Dementation. We prefer all Malkavians to have Dominate and to eliminate Dementation entirely.<br /> <br /> The big problem for me is how to run its effects on characters especially the fifth level. It's hard to know what to do as a PC, how to adjudicate it as an ST, and how to run it so it doesn't just end the game for a character for a long time.<br /> <br /> I think it is an ill-conceived gotcha power whose intent was to make Sabbat Malkavians seem very dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T13:43:59-07:00","id":1492116,"title":"","content":"You're right, these are complaint, my questions:<br /> <br /> Passion: you cannot choose what emotion can be affected but can it be induced? Like &quot;You seems to be annoyed by your compagnon over there, after all he seems like the type to make decisions without consulting you, maybe that hides something&quot; in order to make passion affect anger or distrust<br /> <br /> Can you get rid of it's influence by a therapy, help of friends, or just by realizing we're under influence of Dementation and fight it with willpower roll and/or spent day after day?<br /> <br /> Is the victim aware that he's influenced by someone when Dementation is used on him or is the Discipline discreet enough to not being detected on use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T20:12:25-07:00","id":1492132,"title":"","content":"I share your dislike, although I actually think the opposite: it is ridiculously weak, despite the scary descriptions. It is a pretty bullshit Discipline, and while Malkavian is one of my faves, I never take <b>Dementation</b> Malk for a PC, but I do for NPCs sometimes. So, maybe I can help you reconsider some views, and that may come to improve your game.<br /> <br /> 1 - Of course it has a weakness. Indeed, it has the worse weakness among the &quot;mental powers&quot;, <b>lack of user agency</b>. Most powers are completely or almost completely in the hands of the ST for their effects. Running an NPC it's ok because you're the ST and can use this Discipline as justification to cause any effect you deem interesting for the story, even if it is not what the NPC would chose or benefit from. But as a PC you just get to ask the ST to decide the results, maybe make suggestions with no promises whatsoever;<br /> <br /> 2 - Mental meltdowns of all kinds happen, they're more common than most people think (most people don't talk about them and end up thinking they're weirder than they actually are). So while yes, you may have lingering effects after the preternatural madness ends, specially if you're a recurrent victim, you'll also probably cope with that in some way soon after. Maybe it is a healthy way, maybe it isn't, but the point is that it won't be enough to be a Derangement and will get better with time;<br /> <br /> 3 - Everything you can do with <b>Dementation</b> you can actually do better with <b>Dominate</b> or <b>Presence</b>. Mess with emotion and memory, induce the person to do things they never thought they would, and offer no explanation, a simple Command to cry or laugh out of context can be pretty disturbing if the victim doesn't know what's going on, Mesmerize can cause all sorts of mayhem in someone's life and replicate almost any <b>Dementation</b> effect on its own in some way, the few it can't you get with Forgetful Mind. It is scary to read what <b>Dementation</b> does directly to one's mind, but too easy to do the same and more with other Disciplines;<br /> <br /> 4 - The power itself answers your second actual question within Total Insanity: every time the ST sees reason to allow it (like a therapy session or faced with evidence that a delusion is a delusion, both stated examples) the victim get to spend 1 WP. When you equals the vampire's successes you get over it, regardless of never noticing it was a supernatural power. Knowing that your symptoms may come from a power would reasonably be a way to hasten this process;<br /> <br /> 5 - Following comes a quick breakdown of the powers and my comments on them:<ul><li><b>Passion</b> - On one hand you have <i>some</i> control over the effect, but just because you enhance a pre-existing emotion. To really control it the character would have to act in such a way as to cause the seeding emotion and be sure of it. I would call for an Extended Roll of Intelligence + Empathy for this process, although a simple Perception + Empathy would tell you right away what the current emotion to be affected is;</li> <li><b>The Haunting</b> - No control whatsoever, not even something that can hint to what the effect may come to be, except that it will be &quot;<i>unpleasant and obtrusive</i>&quot;. Enough to <i>maybe</i> cause a dice penalty <i>sometimes</i>, and not even that the user has any control over. That's the power of being annoying, at a level when <b>Dominate</b> can turn you into a mass shooter if you're just a bit nervous and works in a bad environment;</li> <li><b>Eyes of Chaos </b>- The power of understanding people with Occult instead of Empathy because you're hasty, I guess, plus stare at random things when you want to ask the ST pretty please for a Plot Device information from heaven, that the ST only gives if they want to. The single best effect of this is reading secret messages with a static Dif 7 and a single turn, so it isn't completely shit, but it's also level 3, when <b>Dominate</b> lets you mess with memories and <b>Presence</b> completely captures someone's frigging devotion to you;</li> <li><b>Voice of Madness</b> - At least the user has to <i>not choose</i> from just two options, Frenzy or R\u00f6tschreck. No control over what the victims will do with it, either. And on top of that, you target yourself every time and may even end up being the only one affected <i><b>after having a success</b></i>. At this level <b>Dominate</b> can enslave a person for the rest of their life, <b>Animalism</b> can posses animals (and already take other vampires out of a frenzy), and <b>Presence</b> guarantees with a single success that a target anywhere in the world will reach you someday in the relatively near future;</li> <li><b>Total Insanity</b> - While 5 Derangements is a steep penalty, the result is strictly and completely in the ST's hands, and they're still just minor Flaws individually, nothing impossible to work around, they're more a role play challenge than a hindrance. Add to that the option to just burn WP to get rid of it with time and this power will hardly change the outcome of a scene in the way you'd expect from a level 5 effect.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Your greatest challenge with <b>Dementation</b> as an ST is to keep your imagination fresh, because it is a real burden to have to come up with interesting results all on your own every time a player decides to use it. You also bear the whole burden of making it useful or useless, the reason why some players think it is an awesome power while other never got anything worth the effort out of it. I would forbid players getting it on those grounds alone, but otherwise it is really underwhelming. On the hands of an NPC it may work better, specially if you want to add a madness spice to a story but your hands are too full to go with a user of subtler powers creating it little by little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T22:15:11-07:00","id":1492134,"title":"","content":"Dominate Malks should really be the default. <br /> <br /> There is one overlooked weakness in the delivery: The Malkavian has to make an audiable vocalization for the delivery. It's minor, but the victim has a big clue when he goes mad. <br /> <br /> I like Passion, it seems to be very strong, but otherwise Dementation's a waste of XP. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T00:23:37-07:00","id":1492139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492109-need-informations-on-dementation?p=1492134#post1492134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate Malks should really be the default. <br /> <br /> There is one overlooked weakness in the delivery: The Malkavian has to make an audiable vocalization for the delivery. It's minor, but the victim has a big clue when he goes mad. <br /> <br /> I like Passion, it seems to be very strong, but otherwise Dementation's a waste of XP. </div> </div> </div> </div>Personaly i don't share this point, of course dementation isn't as strong as presence and domination at the same level, but a single use on the good person and you can change the entire story's end.<br /> Exemple: The prince is an old vampire, a tyran ruling on his city with cruelty. He has form a group of ally that rule with him, but as the oldest and strongest no one succeeded to defeat or deceive him. One of reasons that allow him to stay on the throne is his paranoia, wich make him keep an eye on his ally to prevent any attempt against him. He has created blood bond on the most usefull and those are the only ones he care of. <br /> Use passion on him to reinforce his paranoia only 1 time at the right time and he will destroy his own empire alone by killing his ally by fear or distrust, making himself vulnerable to an attack.<br /> A mad prince who's been affected by only 1 use of Dementation, that use making his own demons too strong to resist and pushed him to isolate himself, and the biggests injustices he's had made after that pushing Vampires of the city to chase him by hate instead of serving by fear.<br /> <br /> That's how I see the use of Dementation, as the small impulse that free the snow and provoke avalanche, and during this time the real culprit of the chaos has almost no chance to be suspected and just look at his work from outside.<br /> <br /> Dominations force it's victim to act the way his user want, Presence is an emotionnal bond to the user, Dementation can be use descreetly and the result is provoke by the victim herself, she has just been pushed to do it. It's the way of chaos that can weakened your foe not only on their capacity but socially, divide and conquer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 09-02-2022, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T00:30:18-07:00","id":1492141,"title":"","content":"You do realise you can just spend willpower to ignore the power for a turn or two, and do horrible horrible things to anyone trying to abuse it against a major NPC?<br /> <br /> And your scenario is perfectly feasible with mortal means. Manipulation + Empathy does the same thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T01:12:08-07:00","id":1492142,"title":"","content":"I always felt Dementation was nastier then Dominate.<br /> My Sabbat Malk was arguably weak, but no-one messed with him because he could be unpredictable and they didn't want to be his target.<br /> In-pack, Dominate was perceived more as annoying. (sit down, fetch this, shut up). Dementation was feared because it usually would severely fuck your char up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T03:43:27-07:00","id":1492149,"title":"","content":"Use Dementation on the prince and you're fucking dead. Unless you have equal or greater power/backing than him, in which case you would be better off using Dominate or Presence most of the time. Using disciplines in Elysium is also badwrong, unless maybe you're a Nosferatu making yourself more palatable. <br /> <br /> Also, and this is a big strike against Quietus aswell, you can just use regular drugs/poisons to achieve these kinds of things in mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T04:41:55-07:00","id":1492150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492109-need-informations-on-dementation?p=1492139#post1492139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personaly i don't share this point, of course dementation isn't as strong as presence and domination at the same level, but a single use on the good person and you can change the entire story's end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing that can't be said of any other action by a character, supernatural or mundane.<br /> <br /> Think about how much access the perpetrator need in your scenario to begin with, as you have to talk to the Prince to affect them. And you asked if it is subtle: you have to talk to the victim, it takes effect immediately, in a way you can't predict and vampires simply know this power exists already, <b>it isn't subtle</b> even if there's no other telltale for the victim. It's like you suddenly feeling awestruck by another vampire you were indifferent to just moments earlier, there's no Perception roll, but it doesn't take a genius to figure it must have been <b>Presence</b> even if you can't supernaturally prove. It has mundane non-subtlety.<br /> <br /> And you also play directly in the matter of power coming from the ST's interpretation. The Prince has paranoia, yes. But they also lived with it through centuries, past frenzies and trauma and every opportunity within the rules to develop Derangements anyway. And I will stress it, <b>the user has no control over the outcome</b>. Why a character that already deals with this weakness and had been for most of their life would succumb in this specific way? The effects will only play on this cord if the ST decides so, and the character will only succumb so thoroughly if the ST decides so, because otherwise the Discipline has no impact in their ability to make decisions about the symptoms. At the end of the day, <b>the victim will only succumb if the ST so decides, even if the player succeeds on all rolls and has the perfect setup</b>. You presented a compelling reason for the ST to think this result fitting, but if the ST doesn't goes along they simply have not to.<br /> <br /> Your complaint is about the power being disruptive and an &quot;I Win&quot; button. But it is only so if you as an ST decides to make it so, then it is not the power that is dangerous, it's your bias to grant it undue impact. It has a good description and it plays directly into a compelling theme that is madness, but it relies too much into the ST buying into the idea and translating excitement about the theme into tailoring the effects for the player. More importantly, it is a lazy way to dive into the theme, as instead of playing your target's psychology you just shout &quot;go nuts&quot; and they go nuts. You're feeling overburden with a weight you put there yourself by liking its description and hype.<br /> <br /> I do think it is disruptive, but just because of the amount of effort it demands from the ST. The player activates it and you're left with the burden of coming up with an interesting effect out of the blue with no guidance where to go, while interrupting the previous flow of the scene and role play. It is scary, but just because madness is scary (more than it should) and not because it delivers it in a meaningful way. It makes you want to give it gravitas and impact and let you do so freely, but actually has no tool beside the ST's volition and imagination to achieve this.<br /> <br /> On your scenario, a careful character could use other powers or simple guile to affect the Prince's underlings. Spread rumors about their allies betrayal. Make some trusted servants do things the Prince doesn't understand. Have their allies hold irrelevant secrets and then the Prince get wind that they're hiding <i>something</i>. Play the Prince, and the Prince will succumb to their paranoia. If instead you just get near to them and shout &quot;be crazy&quot;, that's just a lazy plan and shouldn't have a major impact, no more than any other Discipline used with similar carelessness. It's dumb, not mad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T06:03:21-07:00","id":1492154,"title":"","content":"So, in summary:<br /> -All you can do through Dementation can be done with other Discipline or even no supernatural powers at all<br /> -you can resist it by spending willpower for a short time (i didn't saw that in my v20 but ok)<br /> -You can never manipulate your target to at least make Passion have better chances to do what we need, the effects are completely random<br /> -if you use it then the victim immediatly realise that something is wrong so any vampire that know that power can guess xho use it<br /> -what happen is entirely up to the st and if the st don't like it or does not know what to do he will just make the victim do what he want<br /> <br /> Then why did they create a Discipline like that at all? If the effect are among tve weakest of all and you have great chance to not have what you need, that Discipline is just roleplay and nothing more<br /> That's... i don't know.... sad, cause it has potential","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T06:39:39-07:00","id":1492156,"title":"","content":"It's not the weakest. Quietus is weak. Dementation... I think it's more a discipline invented for Villains. Like, If you're crazy enough, Dementation is more <i>fun </i>to use than Dominate, and Sabbat Malkavians are crazy. Plus players don't like to be Dominated so making Sabbat Malkavians less effective and more mysterious potentially helps storytellers. Personally, I'd be more open to presence malkavians, but I can see where they were going with Dementation even if I mostly don't like it. I have a few untested character concepts that would work very well as Dementation Malkavians. A character inspired by Batman, for example, would work great as a Dementation Malk.<br /> <br /> I had a thread on dementation somewhere. My conclusion from that: Dementation probably should've been a thaumaturgical path practiced by the Sabbat/Infernalists: I don't think Tremere would be much interested in it. There are several DT paths that I think a madness obsessed malkavian would thrive off: Pleasure, Pain, Fear,<i> Defiler</i>, that one concerning forbidden knowledge... Dementation would work well as one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T06:55:16-07:00","id":1492158,"title":"","content":"I'll echo what others have said. With a player character, Dementation is nearly useless. It lets you become a pain in the ass, but you'd be way better off with Dominate or Presence, because those Disciplines can let you be a pain in the ass too if you're willing to face the consequences of causing trouble, but they also far more useful abilities, especially subtle ones.<br /> <br /> As MWIS mentioned, I think that the idea of Presence Malkavians is really cool. In fact, I think that Presence may well mesh with the theme of insanity more than Dominate is it isn't as strictly controlled, it's about creating passions. I could see an insane person with incredible magnetism like a cult leader.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T07:50:44-07:00","id":1492161,"title":"","content":"As a non Sabbat character, i was imaginating a character that use dementation strategically to weaken his opponents, infiltrating them and using it to sow discord. After all, if I remember correctly, it is one of the disciplines that can be used with enough success when using Domination 5 or Animalism 4, and normally with obfuscate 3.<br /> <br /> But uf you just cannot use it without being caught, cannot induce by manipulation what passion can affect, cannot use it in combat because of it's minimal effects...<br /> <br /> If it's use were discreet enough to have a doubt, like is it really a power or just me going mad because of something, then it could have been extrememy useful for pc for strategical plans to defeat sabbat before any battle, or to weaken a more powerful opponent by affecting him or his ally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T08:04:44-07:00","id":1492162,"title":"","content":"Non-Sabbat characters generally aren't at war. Camarilla vampires have a lot of low intensity conflict but they have a vested interest in keeping such things small so driving someone mad is a good way to escalate things and draw the ire of other vampires. Someone will probably step in and stomp you before your plans make it to fruition.<br /> <br /> Dominate has a lot of good uses: Building up Domains, keeping the masquerade, various miscellanea<br /> Dementation? You can discredit a few people with madness to keep the masquerade but you could do that better with Dominate and rival that with Presence. Passion has some minor uses as a treatment. But most of Dementation is punitive: it's not a nice thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> In a war scenario, rather than drive my enemy mad with a magic power that I need to talk to him to use I'd rather just send armed people/animals his way. Animalism/Dominate/Presence/Vitae/Money are better ways to give me an advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-02-2022, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T09:50:50-07:00","id":1492168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492109-need-informations-on-dementation?p=1492162#post1492162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Sabbat characters generally aren't at war. Camarilla vampires have a lot of low intensity conflict but they have a vested interest in keeping such things small so driving someone mad is a good way to escalate things and draw the ire of other vampires. Someone will probably step in and stomp you before your plans make it to fruition.<br /> <br /> Dominate has a lot of good uses: Building up Domains, keeping the masquerade, various miscellanea<br /> Dementation? You can discredit a few people with madness to keep the masquerade but you could do that better with Dominate and rival that with Presence. Passion has some minor uses as a treatment. But most of Dementation is punitive: it's not a nice thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> In a war scenario, rather than drive my enemy mad with a magic power that I need to talk to him to use I'd rather just send armed people/animals his way. Animalism/Dominate/Presence/Vitae/Money are better ways to give me an advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, still i think Dementation need a rework instead of suppression. If you modify it to be used without risk to be spotted, exchange some power to give short moments of madness, or give it really usefull application (force a target to live again a traumatic experience that will stun him and/or make him loose willpower, increase it's perception difficulty with vision or sound from his past etc...) with as a secondary effect the natural degeneration of his mental health over time, Dementation could become fun, usefull and powerful instead of giving random result that could have been obtain through other Disciplines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T11:18:26-07:00","id":1492175,"title":"","content":"I just ignore Dementation in general and don't even acknowledge it's existence. Why use it when you can achieve the same effects with Dominate and it struck me as an unneeded change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T15:13:59-07:00","id":1492187,"title":"","content":"I think the point of Dementation is that it's disruptive. It's not subtle, it's not directed and it's not predictable. It's a nexus of weirdness and insanity infecting people around you and causing mayhem. It's not about impressing people or giving orders, it's just about raising hell and sharing the madness of the Malkavians with everyone around them.<br /> <br /> It has a very specific narrative purpose and as such it can be used to great effect, but it's just not a straightforward tool.<br /> <br /> I've always found it quite strange that Dementation was the main clan discipline as time went on, especially considering how White Wolf was frowning on fishmalks and trying to stop people from playing the Malkavians like that. Yet, they made the disruptive discipline the main discipline.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T18:24:41-07:00","id":1492193,"title":"","content":"I've always liked the idea of Dementation more than the implementation. The Discipline set feels clunky and I don't feel that it does what it's supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T21:46:07-07:00","id":1492199,"title":"","content":"I think Malkavians can make people go crazy enough through Creative use of Obfuscate, Dominate, and Auspex 4. Mask yourself as their boss/spouse/child/parent/friend and mess with them, force them to do strange acts with command, mesmorize, or give them very strange alterlnatives to their memories with forgetful mind. Dementation's pretty lazy when you think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T01:39:35-07:00","id":1492204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492109-need-informations-on-dementation?p=1492199#post1492199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Malkavians can make people go crazy enough through Creative use of Obfuscate, Dominate, and Auspex 4. Mask yourself as their boss/spouse/child/parent/friend and mess with them, force them to do strange acts with command, mesmorize, or give them very strange alterlnatives to their memories with forgetful mind. Dementation's pretty lazy when you think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but when you put it like that it sounds like something a Ventrue, Tzimisce, or Lasombra would do. Cold, calculated and inhuman just to see how someone will break or how they can push them or punish them. The charm with Dementation is that it's way less personal, way less organised, it's insanity in a box, but you don't really know what it is. It's more Malkavian.<br /> <br /> The powers themselves could probably use some revision and fine tuning, but I've always felt it resonated well with the idea that where Malkavians go madness spreads, and the whole Jerusalem scenario in BJD was well reflective of that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T02:15:39-07:00","id":1492205,"title":"","content":"I think a Ventrue could do it. especially if it became related to their type. I <i>know </i>Lasombra are doing it with their whole Path of Night thing. But Malkavians are uniquely set up with the most optimal discipline spread (Ausp,Dom,Obf) that it becomes their thing, not to mention their weakness. Malkavians are one of the only bloodlines without a physical in-clan discipline, before the advent of explosives they would almost never physically win against their piers and so they would best win by extreme cunning, which is greatly enabled by their discipline spread: having documents go missing, clues lead in circles, allies and retainers turn against you, your reputation tanked in acts you didn't do... you're going to seem mad by the end of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T11:58:20-07:00","id":1492245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492109-need-informations-on-dementation?p=1492154#post1492154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why did they create a Discipline like that at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> hits the nail here. The point with <b>Dementation</b> is the very specific narrative role it plays.<br /> <br /> When you think about doing what you want, that is, to use madness strategically to further a plan, then even mundane methods will serve you better. And if you want to play a character that uses madness with cunning and play on their targets' psychology, then other methods are also more interesting.<br /> <br /> <b>Dementation </b>brings to the table speed and chaos. You hit it and all hell is loose. More importantly, it plays the narrative that madness is contagious, at least Malkavian madness. It is not supposed to make the character effective, but to make them unpredictable. At most it serves as a deterrent, as other people know that messing with you risks a sudden bout of madness that no one knows what will come out of, not even the Malk, so you can't outsmart the user.<br /> <br /> That's not completely useless, but it is extremely niche. In fact, more niche than most gimmicky Disciplines, and that says something. It was meant as a means to make Sabbat Malks more scary precisely by playing this narrative without making them more cunning. Used for its narrow, intended purpose, it's not a bad tool. But outside that, it is too limited. And yes, if you don't want to play a psychological character that takes their time to play their victims like Hannibal Lecter, then <b>Dementation</b> can be lots of fun just by causing mayhem with little effort.<br /> <br /> Now, before changing <b>Dementation</b>, I think it really pays off to consider what a crazy character can do with <b>Dominate </b>and <b>Presence</b>, and that's why as a fan of the Malkavian I think they're better served with their original spread and maybe an OoC <b>Presence</b>. Here is the thing, a player that wants a psychological manipulator will probably have more fun thinking ahead of time how to push a victim's buttons. And a mad character that wants to inflict others with <i>their</i> madness can simply use <b>Dominate</b> to impart the specific beliefs and memories they want. A Malkavian that believes to be in the center of a conspiracy everyone else is a part of can literally use <b>Dominate</b> while in a psychotic state to impart their beliefs on others, make them remember events the vampire believe to be true, and make them the very sleeper agents the vampire believes to exist. Now they do.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it is not that <b>Dementation</b> can't be worked upon. I'm not personally convinced it is badly needed because I am satisfied with other means to achieve the same ends, and I do love the theme of madness myself. In fact, so much that I'm a Psychologist irl, and I'm also very happy at being an autistic not always with a good grasp of the reality neurotypicals seem to live in (it is a very weird and nonsensical reality, it seems). But if you want to do that, you'll have to first delineate your design goals and what set them apart from the other standard Disciplines, as it will have to be something different from the current purpose (that is intrinsically limited). I'll love to see the results anyway, I do think it is a worth endeavor if you're certain of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}